recomp/recomp.py and recomp/runtime.h are derived from nfs-most-wanted-mac
(https://github.com/elforeign/nfs-most-wanted-mac), commit 52247d2b0d9b9039d45500866388c1365203ddea
(2026-11-09). That code is licensed under the MIT License; its license text is kept in
LICENSE.nfs-most-wanted-mac.

Changes made to recomp.py (see scripts/fork_recomp.py):
  - removed the speed.exe code-fingerprint check;
  - the image base is read from the PE header instead of being fixed at 0x400000;
  - the executable path comes from $P3_EXE (or p3_build.py --exe);
  - every NFS Most Wanted address-specific patch is gated behind Recompiler.nfs (False).

runtime.h is unchanged and still declares a few NFS-specific hooks (e.g. car85_count) that this
project does not use.

